arty candidate also on the ballot. Ten independent ratings split between five calling the race a tossup and five leaning Democratic, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 60 percent chance. The only public head-to-head survey, from mid-August, showed Lawrence ahead by two points, but it came from a Democratic sponsor and nothing newer has surfaced.\n\nBarrett enters with a clear money advantage, having raised nearly eight million dollars and holding a large cash edge, and outside groups have spent heavily against Lawrence. Lawrence has drawn national Democratic surrogates including Bernie Sanders and has made data centers his signature issue. A favorable midterm environment for Democrats and the district's even partisan lean make this a narrow Democratic edge heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6941, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6328, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6566, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6287, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7046, "margin": 3.0},